+# Principal continuation: native access, observability, training and Hamilton transport
+
+Goal: advance the owner's five workstreams without replacing the geometric-language-model objective with a count-model benchmark. Base f5fa0977; reuse the prior observer implementation and preserve its original receipts.
+
+## Implementation and acceptance
+1. `learner/lexical_residual.rs`: sparse Fit-only count compilation, artifact-bound Q12 log-add table, independent dyadic count/residual weights, integer Generate mass restoration with Copy/Stop unchanged. Test endpoint parity, malformed bounds/identities, serialization, and rare-token tails. Default serving is unchanged; prototype promotion requires measured usefulness.
+2. `bin/support/principal_continuation.rs`: full 2048-window/114364-target Tune adjudication, fixed candidate grids, calibrated-count/cur-only/unigram/tail/reordered controls, exact dataset identities and mandatory head/tail accounting. All selection uses Tune, not Dev.
+3. Same runner: transport observation at lags 1 through 4 on the exact recorded states; report side information and controls. Exposed development decoding is not a universal memory-capacity bound.
+4. `TlTrainer::from_model_fresh_optimizer`: reconstruct masters from a validated frozen artifact with asserted step-zero equality and reset Adam history explicitly. Run bounded equal-dose learning-rate schedule comparisons with grounded rehearsal and all prior grounded panels reported.
+5. Freeze the selected readout before loading source-disjoint evaluation text. Run same-artifact prediction and actual generation; retain negative outputs. Imported texts bind source URL, licensing and hashes.
+6. `learner/hamilton_transport.rs`: exact Q8 actions on four-component vectors, inverse/composition/norm tests and equal-information ordinary controls. Hamilton product is not synonymous with an energy Hamiltonian; document the skew generator/Hermitian correspondence separately. Do not claim geometric attention solved from these controls.
+
+## Execution safeguards
+No transformer/provider inference; Rust owns data/model computation. Floats are allowed offline, not inside the proposed integer numerical kernel. Exact payload/version ownership remains separate from compressed state. Run tests before implementing new behavior; validate changed paths and retain failed candidates. No changing acceptance after reading final results.
+
+Native and server-side work overlap, but one Cargo build at a time. Local model runs use two threads and projected incremental RAM/storage at most 2 GiB each. Full task projection and standing-authorized allowance are recorded outside the checkout. Preserve 24 GiB plus 128 MiB during execution.
+
+Cleanup removes only recreatable debug output and fully audited duplicate worktree checkouts. Unique uncommitted files are archived and hash-verified before removal; Git commits and branches remain. Target approximately 50 GB free, not deletion at any price.
+
+Delivery: commit named code/evidence/documentation, update current state and plan without dropping history, push a dedicated branch and merge through repository protection. Verify actual origin/main tree, then fast-forward the owner's checkout without overwriting pre-existing edits. CI compatibility acknowledgements are not test execution.
